      "title": "Russian bombing of Ukrainian aid centre kills at least 26, Kyiv says",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/03/russia-bombs-ukrainian-aid-centre-komyshuvakha",
      "description": "<p>Ukrainian president Zelenskyy says attack on aid hub was ‘vile’ and shows Russia does not want to de-escalate</p><p>Russia on Monday bombed an aid distribution centre and neighbouring shelter in southern Ukraine, killing at least 26 ​people, Ukrainian president Volodymyr Zelenskyy and the country’s emergency services said.</p><p>Emergency services said two members of a rescue crew and four police officers were among the dead in the village ⁠of Komyshuvakha, in south-eastern Zaporizhzhia region. Five people were being treated in hospital, including two rescue workers.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/03/russia-bombs-ukrainian-aid-centre-komyshuvakha\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-03T01:13:52"
    },
