    {
      "title": "Russian strikes on Ukrainian aid centre, shelter kill 26, about 20 missing",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/russian-strikes-on-ukrainian-aid-centre-shelter-kill-26-about-20-missing-126110300046_1.html",
      "description": "Russia bombed an aid distribution center and neighboring shelter in southern Ukraine on Monday, killing 26 people, Ukrainian officials said.\nUkrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said in a post on X that strikes first targeted a school building used to distribute humanitarian aid and then took aim at a nearby shelter.\n\"This is further proof that Russia wants no de-escalation,\" Zelenskyy said.\nThe attacks in the village of Komyshuvakha, in the southern Zaporizhzhia region, occurred as a limited ceasefire expired Monday in Kherson, a different region in the country's south. The limited ceasefire agreement had allowed humanitarian aid and evacuation missions into front-line areas in Russian-occupied territory.\n\"There was a moment when the next steps could have shown that progress toward peace was possible,\" Zelenskyy said. \"With these killings, Russia is sending an entirely opposite signal: Russia is counting on more killings.\"\nZelenskyy later said in an address to the nation that",
